** ==============================================================================
** ABAQUS/STANDARD THERMO-MECHANICAL MATERIAL CARD: INCONEL FILLER METAL 82, RAW STATE
** Nickel filler wire ERNiCr-3 (AWS A5.14, ISO 18274 S Ni 6082), weld deposit
** Units: mm, s, tonne, mJ, MPa, C
** Author: Victor Maia (vhfm08@gmail.com)
**
** Material_Inconel82_EA.inp (same values and sources) inside the phase transformation
** framework, so that the filler can start in the raw state (RLS = -1) instead of
** being switched on by *MODEL CHANGE:
**  - the filler is active from the start of the weld; it takes the properties of the
**    deposit when it melts (raw -> liquid at the solidus) and keeps them (solid);
**  - field variable 1 = RLS (-1 raw, 0 liquid, 1 solid); conductivity, elastic
**    modulus and yield stress depend on it, the other properties do not;
**  - raw wire: conductivity 1 % of the deposit (the gap ahead of the beam stays open
**    thermally), E = 214 MPa, yield 1 MPa (quiet element in the stress run);
**    density, specific heat and expansion as the deposit, so the beam heats and
**    melts the wire with its real heat capacity and latent heat;
**  - one solid phase (austenite, fcc), no solid-state transformation;
**  - *INITIAL CONDITIONS, TYPE=SOLUTION on FILLER: -1., 0., 0., 1., then zeros up to the
**    25 SDV of the steel cards (RLS, fGrainColumnar, GrainSize, fPhase_Austenite, ...).
